'''Misato Katsuragi''' is a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]]. She was added in [[Version 8.7 Update#Update 8.7.5|Version 8.7.5]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 489
|rarity = SR
|name1 = Misato Katsuragi
|name2 = Captain Misato
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Captain Misato''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Misato's stats and abilities to an extent reflect those of [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], meaning she does equally well at [[Slow|slowing]] short-ranged Aliens as Castaway/Seafarer does [[Freeze|freezing]] them. The two of them, or otherwise Misato substituting for Castaway, are great help in conquering [[Into the Future]]. From there on, however, Misato's usefulness starts degrading. Castaway's [[True Form]] and [[Talents]] grant him guaranteed [[Survive|Survivor]], a higher proc chance for his more potent ability, giving him an even higher uptime over time, and optional [[Immune to Warp]] as opposed to Misato's rather situational [[Immune to Slow|Slow Immunity]]. Misato's [[Barrier Breaker]] hardly helps as [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] and [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fencer Cat]] are enough to do her job, and better at that. Generally, investing in Seafarer mitigates the need to use Misato for offense and procs as you progress in the game.

